From d4967f5e9c0910c5b75abb081d3bafe981e35054 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hans Bihs <hans.bihs@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:38:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fnpf 6DOF: velocities at the body nodes continued from the
 fluid

velcalc_sig differentiates the body-band values of Fi with 4th-order stencils that reach
two nodes into the body, and at the free-surface node of a footprint column W is Fz from
the extended Fifsf over the body interior.  In the moored-box case (X 311) both gave |U|,
|W| of several m/s alternating from column to column from about 7 s on (body velocity
0.2-0.5 m/s).  These entered the hull loads through the trilinear sampling half a cell off
the hull and umax/wmax (time step, N 61 stop, output).

body_velocities fills U,V,W at the body nodes layer by layer from the fluid (average of the
fluid or already filled neighbours), after the velcalc_sig before the loads of each stage
(level 0 and patches) and after the one at the end of the step (new fnpf_body::velocity
hook in fnpf_RK3/RK4).

Moored box, 2 ranks, 12 s: wmax 4.9 -> 0.98 m/s, umax 0.92 -> 0.55 m/s, motion and loads
close to before, 3 % more run time.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LRtog9ynebDp4TbBnyER9X
